# Modular monolith layout

One Django project, bounded apps with clear boundaries (extractable later).

Apps: accounts, tenancy, founders, events, gatherings, guidebook, membership, payments,
social, chat, store, housing, media, trust, notifications, analytics, adminpanel.

Per-app layout:
- `models.py`         — data only
- `selectors.py`      — read queries (always tenant-aware)
- `services.py`       — write/business logic (transactions, external calls)
- `serializers.py`    — DRF I/O validation
- `views.py`          — thin DRF viewsets
- `urls.py`
- `tasks.py`          — Celery tasks
- `tests/`

Rules:
- No cross-app model imports; call the other app's `services`/`selectors`.
- Settings split: `settings/base.py`, `settings/dev.py`, `settings/prod.py`.